       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error. Sertraline's maximum recommended adult dose is 200 mg per day, and 1000 mg is 5 times that. At that dose there is a serious risk of serotonin syndrome, seizures, QT prolongation and arrhythmia.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **100 mg** by mouth once daily. This is a common maintenance dose.\n- **50 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the usual starting dose for depression and anxiety.\n- **200 mg** by mouth once daily. This is the maximum dose.\n\nIf 1000 mg is intended, please confirm that and give the clinical rationale. I can then enter it with a note, though pharmacy would probably still want to verify it.\n\nOnce you tell me the correct dose, I'll enter the order right away."
